eligibility:
Inclusion Criteria:

* Signed written informed consent prior to any study-related procedures;
* Male or female, aged ≥ 18 years;
* Cohort 1: Histologically confirmed gastric or gastroesophageal junction adenocarcinoma, locally advanced per AJCC 8th edition, cTNM stage cT2-4N+M0 by endoscopic ultrasound or contrast-enhanced CT/MRI (with endoscopic ultrasonography and diagnostic laparoscopic exploration if necessary), and assessed as resectable by the investigator;
* Cohort 2: Histopathologically confirmed unresectable advanced or metastatic gastric or gastroesophageal junction adenocarcinoma, cTNM stage cT4bN+M0/1 by endoscopic ultrasound or contrast-enhanced CT/MRI (with endoscopic ultrasonography and diagnostic laparoscopic exploration if necessary) (M1 defined as presence of distant metastasis, including but not limited to oligometastasis and extensive metastasis);
* No prior systemic treatment for the current disease, including surgery, antitumor radiotherapy/chemotherapy/immunotherapy;
* MSI-H by microsatellite instability testing (using the 5 microsatellite loci recommended by the National Cancer Institute: BAT25, BAT26, NR21, NR24, NR27, or other guideline- and clinically-recognized locus combinations) or dMMR by mismatch repair testing (expression of the 4 common MMR proteins MLH1, MSH2, MSH6, and PMS2 by immunohistochemistry, with positive expression localized in the nucleus);
* Agreement to undergo radical surgery and no surgical contraindications as judged by the surgeon (Cohort 1);
* ECOG performance status 0-1;
* No serious concomitant diseases threatening survival (expected survival time \< 5 years);
* Adequate organ function, meeting the following laboratory criteria: Bone marrow function: absolute neutrophil count (ANC) ≥ 1.5×10⁹/L; platelet count ≥ 90×10⁹/L; hemoglobin \> 80 g/L; Total bilirubin ≤ 1.5×ULN (≤ 3×ULN for participants with Gilbert's syndrome or liver metastasis); if total bilirubin \> 1.5×ULN or 3×ULN but direct bilirubin ≤ ULN, enrollment also permitted; AST and ALT ≤ 2.5×ULN (≤ 5.0×ULN for patients with liver metastasis); Serum creatinine ≤ 1.5×ULN and creatinine clearance (Cockcroft-Gault formula) ≥ 50 mL/min; Good coagulation function, defined as INR or PT ≤ 1.5×ULN; certain anticoagulants (e.g., antiplatelet agents, vitamin K antagonists) discontinued 7-14 days before surgery and replaced with other drugs (e.g., low molecular weight heparin);
* At least one measurable lesion per RECIST v1.1;
* For women of childbearing potential, negative urine or serum pregnancy test within 3 days before first dose of study drug (Day 1 of Cycle 1); serum pregnancy test required if urine result cannot be confirmed as negative; non-childbearing potential defined as at least 1 year postmenopausal, or surgical sterilization or hysterectomy;
* For all participants (male or female) with risk of conception, contraceptive measures with an annual failure rate \< 1% throughout treatment until 120 days after last dose of study drug (or 180 days after last dose of chemotherapy).

Exclusion Criteria:

* Prior receipt of any antitumor therapy for the study disease, including surgery, radiotherapy, chemotherapy, targeted therapy, immunotherapy;
* Prior receipt of anti-PD-1, anti-PD-L1, anti-programmed death ligand 2 (PD-L2), or anti-cytotoxic T lymphocyte-associated antigen 4 (CTLA-4) agents, or any other agents acting on T-cell costimulatory or immune checkpoint pathways (e.g., OX40, CD137, etc.), or adoptive cell immunotherapy;
* Concurrent participation in another clinical study, unless participating in an observational (non-interventional) clinical study or in the survival follow-up phase of an interventional study;
* Receipt of any investigational drug or investigational device therapy within 4 weeks before the first dose of study drug;
* Major surgery (e.g., craniotomy, thoracotomy, or laparotomy) within 4 weeks before the first dose of study drug, anticipated need for major surgery during the study treatment period (except radical gastrectomy specified in the protocol), or presence of unhealed wounds, ulcers, or fractures; exploratory surgery for tumor staging is permitted;
* Use of immunosuppressive drugs within 4 weeks before the first dose of study drug, excluding: Intranasal inhaled local steroid therapy or local steroid injection (e.g., intra-articular injection); Systemic corticosteroid therapy not exceeding 10 mg/day prednisone or its equivalent physiological dose; Corticosteroids as prophylaxis for allergic reactions (e.g., premedication before CT);
* Receipt of Chinese patent medicine with antitumor indications or drugs with immunomodulatory effects (including thymosin, interferon, interleukin, excluding local use for control of pleural effusion) as systemic treatment within 2 weeks before the first dose;
* Active autoimmune disease requiring systemic treatment (e.g., disease-modifying drugs, corticosteroids, or immunosuppressants) within 2 years before the first dose; replacement therapy (e.g., thyroxine, insulin, or physiological corticosteroids for adrenal or pituitary insufficiency) is not considered systemic treatment;
* History of other primary malignancies, excluding: Cured malignancy with no known active disease and very low risk of recurrence ≥ 2 years before the first dose of study drug; Adequately treated non-melanoma skin cancer or lentigo maligna with no evidence of disease recurrence; Adequately treated carcinoma in situ with no evidence of disease recurrence;
* Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infection (HIV antibody positive);
* Acute or chronic active hepatitis B (defined as HBsAg positive, or HBcAb positive alone with HBV DNA ≥ 2000 IU/mL or ≥ 1×10⁴ copies/mL), or acute or chronic active hepatitis C (defined as HCV antibody positive with HCV-RNA level above the lower limit of detection);
* Known history of primary immunodeficiency;
* Interstitial lung disease requiring treatment; prior or current pulmonary diseases such as pulmonary fibrosis, pneumoconiosis, drug-related pneumonia, organic pneumonia (e.g., bronchiolitis obliterans), or severe impairment of pulmonary function;
* Known allogeneic organ transplantation (except corneal transplantation) or allogeneic hematopoietic stem cell transplantation;
* Presence of any serious or uncontrolled systemic disease, such as: Resting electrocardiogram showing major and severe symptomatic uncontrolled abnormalities in rhythm, conduction, or morphology, such as complete left bundle branch block, second-degree or higher heart block, ventricular arrhythmia, or atrial fibrillation with poorly controlled ventricular rate (ventricular rate \> 110 beats/min); Poorly controlled unstable angina, congestive heart failure, or chronic heart failure of New York Heart Association (NYHA) class ≥ 2; History of deep vein thrombosis, pulmonary embolism, cerebral infarction, or any other serious thromboembolic event within 3 months before the first dose of study drug (implantable venous access port or catheter-related thrombosis, or superficial vein thrombosis is not considered a "serious" thromboembolic event); Poorly controlled blood pressure (systolic blood pressure \> 140 mmHg, diastolic blood pressure \> 90 mmHg); Active pulmonary tuberculosis; Active or uncontrolled infection requiring systemic treatment; Severe bleeding tendency or coagulation disorder, or currently receiving thrombolytic therapy; Presence of gastrointestinal obstruction; Liver diseases such as cirrhosis, decompensated liver disease, acute or chronic active hepatitis; Poorly controlled diabetes (fasting blood glucose (FBG) \> 10 mmol/L); Urine protein ≥ 3+ on urinalysis, with confirmed 24-hour urinary protein \> 1.0 g; Presence of psychiatric disorders preventing cooperation with treatment;
* Known allergy to the drugs used in this study;
* Pregnant or breastfeeding women;
* History or evidence of disease, treatment, or abnormal laboratory values that may interfere with study results, prevent full participation in the study, or any other condition considered unsuitable for enrollment by the investigator; presence of other potential risks considered unsuitable for participation in this study by the investigator.

Inclusion Criteria:

1. Have a thorough understanding of this study and have voluntarily signed the informed consent form;
2. Age between 18 and 65 years old, male or female;
3. Patients with unresectable locally advanced or metastatic gastric/esophageal gastroesophageal junction adenocarcinoma confirmed by pathological or histological examination;
4. ECOG physical condition score of 0-1;
5. Expected survival of ≥ 3 months;
6. Have not received any anti-tumor treatment (including chemotherapy, targeted therapy, immunotherapy, etc.) for unresectable locally advanced or metastatic gastric cancer before (including any adjuvant treatment after gastric cancer radical surgery, provided that the time from the end of the last adjuvant chemotherapy to the discovery of metastatic disease is greater than 6 months);
7. Have at least one measurable lesion (meets RECIST v1.1 criteria);
8. The functions of important organs meet the following requirements (do not use any blood components, and cell growth factors within 14 days before enrollment):

   * Absolute neutrophil count (ANC) ≥ 1.5 × 10\^9/L; platelets ≥ 100 × 10\^9/L; hemoglobin ≥ 90 g/L;
   * Total bilirubin ≤ 1.5 × upper limit of normal (ULN); aspartate aminotransferase (AST), alanine aminotransferase (ALT) ≤ 5.0 × ULN; albumin ≥ 30 g/L
   * Serum creatinine ≤ 1.5 × ULN and creatinine clearance rate (calculated using the Cockcroft-Gault formula) ≥ 60 ml/min;
   * Good coagulation function, and need to meet the following conditions: international normalized ratio (INR) ≤ 1.5 (for those not receiving anticoagulation treatment); prothrombin time (PT) ≤ 1.5 × ULN; activated partial thromboplastin time (APTT) ≤ 1.5 × ULN;
   * Normal thyroid function, defined as thyroid stimulating hormone (TSH) within the normal range. (If the baseline TSH is outside the normal range, and total T3 (or FT3) and FT4 are within the normal range, and there are no clinical symptoms, they can also be enrolled);
   * No active bleeding, such as hematemesis, hematochezia, gingival bleeding, epistaxis, and hemorrhage from hemorrhoids, and fecal occult blood ≤ +; gastroscopy shows no high bleeding risk of the primary lesion (such as exposed blood vessels at the ulcer base);
9. Patients with potential fertility need to use a medically approved contraceptive method (such as intrauterine device, contraceptive pills, or condoms) during the study treatment and within 1 month after the end of the study treatment; and the serum or urine HCG test must be negative within 72 hours before enrollment, and must be non-lactating.

Exclusion Criteria:

1. Patients with a known HER-2 status as positive (immunohistochemistry 3+, or, immunohistochemistry 2+ and FISH positive);
2. Those who had other malignant tumors within 5 years before enrollment, including skin basal cell or squamous cell carcinoma after radical surgery, or cervical carcinoma in situ, excluding;
3. Those who had received allogeneic bone marrow transplantation or organ transplantation in the past;
4. Those who had severe cardiovascular diseases within 6 months before enrollment, including unstable angina pectoris or myocardial infarction;
5. Subjects who were allergic to the study drug or any of its auxiliary preparations;
6. Those who had uncontrolled hypertension before enrollment, defined as: systolic blood pressure ≥ 150 mmHg and/or diastolic blood pressure ≥ 90 mmHg;
7. Those who had any disease or condition that affected drug absorption before enrollment, or who could not take the drug orally;
8. Those who had active peptic ulcers in the stomach and duodenum, ulcerative colitis, or active bleeding from any unresected tumor, or conditions that the investigator judged might cause gastrointestinal bleeding or perforation;
9. Those who had clear evidence or history of significant bleeding within 3 months before enrollment (3-month bleeding \> 30 mL, accompanied by hematemesis, melena, or bloody stool), hemoptysis (fresh blood \> 5 mL within 4 weeks), or a thromboembolic event within 12 months (including stroke events and/or transient ischemic attacks);
10. Those with significant clinical cardiovascular diseases, including but not limited to acute myocardial infarction within 6 months before enrollment, severe/ unstable angina pectoris or coronary artery bypass surgery; congestive heart failure with NYHA classification \> 2; drug-induced ventricular arrhythmias; LVEF (left ventricular ejection fraction) \< 50%;
11. Active or uncontrolled severe infections (≥ CTCAE v5.0 grade 2 infection);
12. Known human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infection. Those with a clinically significant history of liver disease, including viral hepatitis \[for those known to be HBV carriers, active HBV infection must be excluded, i.e., HBV DNA positive (\> 1×104 copies/mL or \> 2000 IU/ml); known hepatitis C infection (HCV) and HCV RNA positive (\> 1×103 copies/mL)\];
13. Patients with any active autoimmune disease or a history of autoimmune disease (as listed below, but not limited to: autoimmune hepatitis, interstitial pneumonia, uveitis, enteritis, hepatitis, pituitaryitis, vasculitis, nephritis, hyperthyroidism; patients with vitiligo; those who had complete remission of childhood asthma and no intervention required after adulthood can be included; patients with bronchial asthma requiring medical intervention cannot be included); alternative treatments are not considered systemic treatments; the following patients can be included: those with autoimmune-related hypothyroidism who received thyroid hormone replacement therapy; those with type 1 diabetes that can be controlled with insulin therapy;
14. Those who used immunosuppressants or systemic hormone therapy to achieve immunosuppression purposes within 7 days before enrollment (dose \> 10mg/day prednisone or other equivalent efficacy hormones);
15. Those who currently have interstitial lung disease or pneumonia, pulmonary fibrosis, acute pulmonary diseases, radiation pneumonia;
16. Pregnant (positive pregnancy test before medication) or lactating women;
17. Any other diseases, clinically significant metabolic abnormalities, physical examination abnormalities or laboratory test abnormalities, as judged by the investigator, suggesting that the patient has a certain disease or condition that is not suitable for using the study drug (such as having epilepsy and requiring treatment), or will affect the interpretation of the study results, or place the patient at a high risk;
18. Urinalysis indicates that urine protein is ≥ 2+, and the 24-hour urine protein volume is \> 1.0g;
19. Other acute or chronic diseases, mental disorders, or abnormal laboratory test results that may lead to the following outcomes: increase the risk of participating in the study or receiving the study drug, or interfere with the interpretation of the study results, and according to the researcher's judgment, patients classified as not eligible to participate in this study are considered unsuitable for inclusion by the researcher;
20. Participating in another interventional clinical study at the same time, unless participating in an observational (non-interventional) clinical study or in the follow-up stage of an interventional study; patients considered not suitable for inclusion in this study by the researcher.

Inclusion Criteria:

* Patients aged 18-75 years with gastric or gastroesophageal junction adenocarcinoma, male or female;
* According to the AJCC 8th edition gastric cancer staging, patients assessed by abdominal CT as cStage III (cT3-4aN1-3M0), and diagnosed with gastric or gastroesophageal junction adenocarcinoma by gastroscopy and pathology; for gastroesophageal junction (GEJ) cancer, only Siewert type III and Siewert type II subjects who do not require combined thoracotomy are allowed to be enrolled.
* Before enrollment, after joint assessment by a attending gastrointestinal surgeon and an imaging technician, the tumor is determined to be cStage III and the patient is eligible for curative-intent R0 resection; the patient agrees to undergo radical surgery and is judged by the surgeon to have no surgical contraindications;
* No prior systemic therapy for the current disease, including surgery, anti-tumor radiotherapy/chemotherapy/immunotherapy, etc.;
* Expected survival ≥6 months;
* Measurable tumor lesions according to RECIST v1.1 criteria (see Appendix 1);
* ECOG PS score (see Appendix 2) of 0-1 within 7 days before the first dose;
* Good cardiac function and suitable for curative-intent resection. If clinically indicated, patients with underlying ischemic, valvular heart disease, or other severe heart disease should undergo preoperative evaluation by a cardiologist;
* Normal function of major organs; subjects must meet the following laboratory criteria:

  1. Absolute neutrophil count (ANC) ≥1.5×10⁹/L without the use of granulocyte colony-stimulating factor within the past 14 days;
  2. Platelet count ≥100×10⁹/L without blood transfusion within the past 14 days;
  3. Total bilirubin ≤1.5× upper limit of normal (ULN); if total bilirubin \>1.5×ULN but direct bilirubin ≤ULN, enrollment is also permitted;
  4. Aspartate aminotransferase (AST) and alanine aminotransferase (ALT) ≤2.5×ULN;
  5. Serum creatinine ≤1.5×ULN and creatinine clearance (calculated using the Cockcroft-Gault formula) ≥60 mL/min;
  6. Good coagulation function, defined as international normalized ratio (INR) or prothrombin time (PT) ≤1.5×ULN;
  7. Normal thyroid function, defined as thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) within the normal range. If baseline TSH is outside the normal range, subjects with total T3 (or FT3) and FT4 within the normal range may also be enrolled;
  8. Myocardial enzyme spectrum within the normal range (if the investigator comprehensively judges it as a clinically insignificant isolated laboratory abnormality, enrollment is also permitted); Thyroid function indicators: thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH), free thyroxine (FT3/FT4) within the normal range or with mild and clinically insignificant abnormalities; Body weight above 40 kg (including 40 kg), or BMI \>18.5;
* Female patients must meet:

  1. Postmenopausal status (defined as no menstruation for at least 1 year, with no other confirmed cause other than menopause), or have undergone surgical sterilization (oophorectomy and/or hysterectomy), or patients of childbearing potential must simultaneously meet the following requirements:
  2. Pregnancy test within 7 days before the first dose must be negative;
  3. Agree to use contraceptive measures with an annual failure rate \<1% or maintain abstinence (avoid heterosexual intercourse) (from signing the informed consent form until at least 120 days after the last dose of the study drug, and at least 9 months after surgery) (contraceptive methods with an annual failure rate \<1% include bilateral tubal ligation, male sterilization, correct use of hormonal contraceptives that inhibit ovulation, hormone-releasing intrauterine devices, and copper-containing intrauterine devices.);
  4. Must not breastfeed.
* Male patients must meet:

Agree to abstinence (avoid heterosexual intercourse) or use contraceptive measures, as specified below: when the partner is a woman of childbearing potential or the partner is pregnant, male patients must maintain abstinence or correctly use condoms for at least 120 days after the last dose of the study drug and at least 9 months after surgery. The reliability of sexual abstinence should be evaluated with reference to the duration of the clinical study, patient preference, and daily lifestyle. Periodic abstinence (e.g., calendar days, ovulation period, basal...)

* Subjects read and fully understand the patient information and sign the informed consent form.

Exclusion Criteria:

* Patients with a prior (within 5 years) or concurrent other malignancy. Cured localized tumors, such as basal cell carcinoma of the skin, squamous cell carcinoma of the skin, superficial bladder cancer, carcinoma in situ of the prostate, carcinoma in situ of the cervix, carcinoma in situ of the breast, stage I lung cancer, stage I colorectal cancer, etc., may be enrolled;
* Patients preparing to undergo or having previously received organ or bone marrow transplantation;
* Any bleeding event of severity grade 3 or above according to CTCAE 5.0 occurring within 4 weeks before screening;
* Abnormal coagulation function with a bleeding tendency (INR \>1.5 of the normal value without the use of anticoagulants); patients treated with anticoagulants or vitamin K antagonists such as warfarin, heparin, or their analogues; on the premise that the prothrombin time international normalized ratio (INR) ≤1.5, low-dose warfarin (1 mg orally, once daily) or low-dose aspirin (daily dose not exceeding 100 mg) for prophylactic purposes is permitted;
* Occurrence of arterial/venous thrombotic events within 6 months before screening, such as cerebrovascular accident (including transient ischemic attack), deep vein thrombosis (except those caused by venous catheterization due to prior chemotherapy and judged by the investigator to have healed), and pulmonary embolism, etc.;
* Occurrence of myocardial infarction or poorly controlled arrhythmia (including QTc interval ≥450 ms in males and ≥470 ms in females) within 6 months before the first dose (QTc interval calculated using the Fridericia formula);
* Presence of NYHA class III-IV cardiac insufficiency or echocardiography: LVEF (left ventricular ejection fraction) \<50%;
* Urinalysis indicating urine protein ≥++ and confirmed 24-hour urine protein quantification \>1.0 g;
* Presence of multiple factors affecting oral medication (such as inability to swallow, chronic diarrhea, and intestinal obstruction, etc.);
* Symptomatic pleural effusion or ascites requiring clinical intervention;
* Human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infection;
* Active pulmonary tuberculosis;
* Long-term non-healing wounds or incompletely healed fractures;
* Prior and current interstitial pneumonia, pneumoconiosis, radiation pneumonia, drug-related pneumonia, severe impairment of pulmonary function, etc., which may interfere with the detection and management of suspected drug-related pulmonary toxicity;
* Presence of known active or suspected autoimmune disease, except those in a stable state of the disease at enrollment (not requiring systemic immunosuppressive therapy);
* History of severe chronic autoimmune disease, such as systemic lupus erythematosus, etc.; history of inflammatory bowel disease such as ulcerative colitis and Crohn's disease; history of chronic diarrheal diseases such as irritable bowel syndrome; history of sarcoidosis or tuberculosis; history of active hepatitis B, hepatitis C, and HIV infection; well-controlled non-severe immune diseases such as dermatitis, arthritis, psoriasis, etc., may be enrolled. Hepatitis B virus titer \<500 copies/mL may be enrolled;
* Patients requiring systemic corticosteroids (\>10 mg/day prednisone-equivalent dose) or other immunosuppressive therapy within 14 days before the first dose or during the study period. However, the following conditions are permitted for enrollment: in the absence of active autoimmune disease, patients are permitted to use topical or inhaled steroids, or adrenal hormone replacement therapy at a dose ≤10 mg/day prednisone-equivalent dose;
* Any active infection requiring systemic anti-infective treatment within 14 days before the first dose; except for receiving prophylactic antibiotic treatment (such as prevention of urinary tract infection or chronic obstructive pulmonary disease);
* Treatment with live vaccines within 28 days before the first dose; except for inactivated viral vaccine treatment for seasonal influenza;
* Prior treatment with antibody/drug therapy targeting immune checkpoints, such as PD-1, PD-L1, CTLA-4 inhibitors, etc.;
* Treatment with immune-related drugs or medical technologies within 6 months before the first dose (including but not limited to the following: thymopentin, thymalfasin, interferon, CAR-T therapy, etc.);
* Currently receiving other drug-related clinical study treatment, or the planned start time of this study treatment is less than 1 month from the end of the previous drug-related clinical study treatment;
* Known history of allergy or intolerance to any study drug or its components;
* Patients with a history of alcoholism, drug use, and drug abuse. Patients who have stopped drinking alcohol may be enrolled;
* Patients with non-compliance with medical advice, non-compliance with prescribed medication, or incomplete data, etc., which may affect the assessment of efficacy or safety;
* Pregnant or lactating female patients;
* Patients with conditions that may increase the risk of participating in the study and study drug use, or other severe, acute, and chronic diseases, who, as judged by the investigator, are not suitable for participation in clinical research.
* Other circumstances judged by the investigator as unsuitable for this clinical trial.

Inclusion Criteria:

* Fully understand this study and voluntarily sign the informed consent form, with good compliance and cooperation with follow-up;
* Age ≥18 years;
* Eastern Cooperative Oncology Group（ECOG） score 0-1;
* Histologically or cytologically confirmed gastric adenocarcinoma or gastroesophageal junction adenocarcinoma, locally advanced and unresectable, with local recurrence or distant metastasis;
* Immunohistochemistry (IHC) testing for Her2 expression: IHC3+ or IHC2+;
* First-line standard treatment failure in gastric adenocarcinoma or gastroesophageal junction adenocarcinoma: (1) postoperative recurrence or metastasis patients progressing during concurrent chemoradiotherapy; (2) for neoadjuvant/adjuvant therapy containing immunotherapy, if patients progress during treatment or within 6 months after treatment, it is also considered first-line treatment failure;
* Patients must have at least one measurable lesion (according to RECIST 1.1 criteria);
* Major organ functions are normal, meeting the following criteria:(1) Blood routine test standards must meet (no blood transfusion or blood products, and no use of G-CSF or other hematopoietic stimulating factors within 14 days to correct): A. Hemoglobin (Hb) ≥90 g/L; B. Absolute neutrophil count (ANC) ≥1.5 ×10\^9/L; C. Platelet count (PLT) ≥80×10\^9/L; (2) Biochemical tests must meet the following standards: A. Total bilirubin (TBIL) \<1.5 × upper limit of normal (ULN);B. Alanine aminotransferase (ALT) and aspartate aminotransferase (AST) \<2.5 ULN, or \<5 ULN for patients with liver metastasis; C. Serum creatinine (Cr) ≤1.5 ULN or estimated creatinine clearance \>60 ml/min (Cockcroft-Gault formula); D. Urinalysis results: urine protein (UPRO) \<2 or 24-hour urine protein \<1 g; (3) Doppler ultrasound evaluation: left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) ≥ lower limit of normal (50%); (4) Coagulation: international normalized ratio (INR) ≤1.5×ULN and activated partial thromboplastin time ≤1.5×ULN;(5) Pulmonary function: forced expiratory volume in 1 second (FEV1) ≥1.2 L, FEV1% ≥70%, carbon monoxide diffusing capacity (DLCO) ≥50%; (6) Cardiac chocardiography: left ventricular ejection fraction (LVEF) ≥50%;(7) Electrocardiogram Fridericia-corrected QT interval (QTcF): women \<470 ms, men \<450 ms; (8) Others: lipase ≤1.5×ULN (if lipase \>1.5×ULN without clinical or imaging evidence of pancreatitis, enrollment is allowed); amylase ≤1.5×ULN (if amylase \>1.5×ULN without clinical or imaging evidence of pancreatitis, enrollment is allowed); alkaline phosphatase (ALP) ≤2.5×ULN.
* Women of childbearing potential must agree to use effective contraception during the study and for 6 months after the study; must have a negative serum or urine pregnancy test within 7 days before enrollment, and must not be breastfeeding; men must agree to use contraception during the study and for 6 months after the study.

Exclusion Criteria:

* Known allergy to any investigational drug or its excipients, or allergy to humanized monoclonal antibody products (such as trastuzumab, pertuzumab, etc.).
* (1) Received any investigational drug within 4 weeks before the first use of the study drug; (2) subjects who require systemic treatment with corticosteroids (daily dose \>10 mg prednisone equivalent) or other immunosuppressants within 2 weeks before the first use of the study drug, except for using corticosteroids for local esophageal inflammation, allergy prevention, or nausea and vomiting; (3) other special situations need to be discussed with the sponsor. In the absence of active autoimmune disease, inhaled or local steroids and adrenal corticosteroid replacement at doses \>10 mg/day prednisone equivalent are allowed; (4) subjects who have received anti-cancer vaccines or live vaccines within 4 weeks before the first administration of the study drug.
* Having any active autoimmune disease or a history of autoimmune disease (such as interstitial pneumonia, uveitis, enteritis, hepatitis, hypophysitis, vasculitis, myocarditis, nephritis, hyperthyroidism, hypothyroidism), except for vitiligo or childhood asthma/allergies that have resolved and require no intervention in adulthood; autoimmune-mediated hypothyroidism treated with a stable dose of thyroid replacement hormone and type 1 diabetes patients using a stable dose of insulin can be included.
* History of immunodeficiency, including positive HIV test, or having other acquired or congenital immunodeficiency diseases, or a history of organ transplant or allogeneic bone marrow transplantation.
* Uncontrolled clinical symptoms or diseases of the heart, such as (1) NYHA II or higher heart failure, (2) unstable angina, (3) myocardial infarction within 1 year, (4) clinically significant supraventricular or ventricular arrhythmias requiring medical intervention.
* Severe infection (CTCAE \> Grade 2) within 4 weeks before first use of the study drug, such as severe pneumonia requiring hospitalization, bacteremia, or infections with complications; baseline chest imaging indicating active lung inflammation; symptoms or signs of infection within 2 weeks before first use of the study drug requiring oral or intravenous antibiotics, except for prophylactic antibiotic use; history of interstitial lung disease, non-infectious pneumonia, pulmonary fibrosis, or other uncontrolled acute lung diseases; active pulmonary tuberculosis found by history or CT, or a history of active pulmonary tuberculosis within 1 year before enrollment, or a history of active pulmonary tuberculosis over 1 year ago but not properly treated; subjects with active hepatitis B (HBV DNA ≥2000 IU/mL or 104 copies/mL) or hepatitis C (HCV antibody positive and HCV-RNA above the detection limit of the assay).
* Before using the study drug for the first time, diagnosed with any other malignant tumor is excluded, except for those with low risk of metastasis and death (5-year survival rate \>90%), such as fully treated basal cell or squamous cell skin cancer or cervical carcinoma in situ.
* Pregnant or breastfeeding women; subjects of reproductive potential who are unwilling or unable to use effective contraception.
* Patients who, in the investigator's judgment, are considered not suitable to enroll.

Inclusion Criteria:

* Age ≥18 years;
* Confirmed diagnosis of chronic obstructive pulmonary disease (COPD);
* Scheduled for elective sedated gastroenteroscopy (gastroscopy, colonoscopy, or combined gastroscopy and colonoscopy);
* Expected procedure duration ≤45 minutes;
* Provision of written informed consent by the participant.

Exclusion Criteria:

* Patients with absolute contraindications to high-flow therapy, including but not limited to confirmed diagnosis of complete upper airway obstruction, basilar skull fracture or nasal bone fracture, pneumothorax, or pneumomediastinum.;
* American Society of Anesthesiologists (ASA) Physical Status class ≥ IV;
* Requirement for planned endotracheal intubation;
* Existing tracheostomy;
* Confirmed pregnancy or currently breastfeeding;
* Known allergy to sedative agents such as propofol;
* Current participation in another interventional clinical trial;
* Any other condition deemed by the investigator to make the patient unsuitable for trial participation.

Inclusion Criteria:

* Age ≥ 18 years; Open to all genders;
* Patients with a definitive histopathological diagnosis of gastric adenocarcinoma or gastroesophageal junction adenocarcinoma, and an ECOG score ≤ 2;
* Gastric cancer or gastroesophageal junction cancer with TNM stage IB-II;
* HER-2-positive (IHC 3+ or IHC 2+ with amplification confirmed by FISH/SISH/CISH);
* Tumor resection has been completed, and adjuvant therapy is planned postoperatively;
* Adequate organ function; participants must meet the following laboratory criteria:
* Absolute neutrophil count (ANC) ≥ 1.5 × 10⁹/L, without the use of granulocyte colony-stimulating factor (G-CSF) within the past 14 days;
* Platelet count ≥ 100 × 10⁹/L, without a blood transfusion within the past 14 days;
* Hemoglobin \> 9 g/dL, without a blood transfusion or the use of erythropoietin within the past 14 days;
* Total bilirubin ≤ 1.5 × upper limit of normal (ULN);
* Aspartate aminotransferase (AST) and alanine aminotransferase (ALT) ≤ 2.5 × ULN;
* Serum creatinine ≤ 1.5 × ULN and creatinine clearance (calculated using the Cockcroft-Gault formula) ≥ 60 mL/min;
* Normal coagulation function, defined as an International Normalized Ratio (INR) or prothrombin time (PT) ≤ 1.5 times the ULN;
* Normal thyroid function, defined as thyroid-stimulating hormone (TSH) within the normal range. If baseline TSH is outside the normal range, subjects may still be enrolled provided that total T3 (or FT3) and FT4 are within the normal range;
* Cardiac enzyme levels are within the normal range (participants with isolated laboratory abnormalities deemed clinically insignificant by the investigator's comprehensive assessment may also be enrolled);
* Voluntary participation in the study and signing of an informed consent form prior to study initiation.

Exclusion Criteria:

* Other malignant tumors of the stomach;
* Received, prior to screening, or is scheduled to receive during the trial any anticancer therapy other than the chemotherapy regimen specified in the protocol (e.g., radiation therapy, targeted therapy, immunotherapy);
* Has or has had a malignant tumor in any other part of the body (except for adequately treated cervical carcinoma in situ, basal cell carcinoma of the skin, or other tumors that have been surgically cured and have not recurred for at least 5 years);
* Presence of any severe or uncontrolled systemic disease, such as:
* Unstable angina, congestive heart failure, or chronic heart failure classified as New York Heart Association (NYHA) Class ≥ 2;
* Significant and symptomatic, difficult-to-control abnormalities in rhythm, conduction, or morphology on a resting electrocardiogram, such as complete left bundle branch block, second-degree or higher heart block, ventricular arrhythmias, or atrial fibrillation;
* Any arterial thrombosis, embolism, or ischemia occurring within 6 months prior to enrollment, such as myocardial infarction, unstable angina, cerebrovascular accident, or transient ischemic attack;
* Poorly controlled blood pressure (systolic blood pressure \> 150 mmHg, diastolic blood pressure \> 100 mmHg);
* A history of non-infectious pneumonia requiring glucocorticoid therapy within 1 year prior to the first dose, or current clinically active interstitial lung disease;
* Active pulmonary tuberculosis;
* Active or uncontrolled infection requiring systemic treatment;
* Clinically active diverticulitis, intra-abdominal abscess, or gastrointestinal obstruction;
* Liver disease, such as cirrhosis, decompensated liver disease, or acute or chronic active hepatitis;
* Poorly controlled diabetes (fasting blood glucose (FBG) \> 10 mmol/L);
* Patients with urine protein ≥++ on urinalysis and confirmed 24-hour urine protein quantification \> 1.0 g;
* Patients with psychiatric disorders who are unable to comply with treatment;
* Patients currently participating in other clinical trials or who have participated in other clinical trials within the past 3 months;
* Patients with known allergies to the medications used in this study;
* Patients deemed unsuitable for participation in this clinical trial by the investigator.

Inclusion Criteria:

* For healthy subjects:

  * 18 years of age or older;
  * Deemed healthy at screening visit based on the following assessments: physical examination, height and weight, medical history, and blood pressure, pulse, temperature, pulse oximetry, heart rhythm, and respiratory rate. labs within the previous month can be utilized to determine eligibility;
  * No known history of atrial fibrillation with CHA₂DS₂-VASc score of 1 or higher, or history of thrombosis;
  * Negative drug screen;
  * Have the ability to give written informed consent.
